{
  "schema_version": "3.0",
  "key": "genitive",
  "concept_slug": "genitive",
  "grounding_mode": "fallback_no_wiki",
  "title": "Showing Ownership with -s and til",
  "cefr_level": "A2",
  "goal": "Use Norwegian -s and til patterns to show who owns or is connected to something.",
  "elements": [
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "orient",
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The genitive is a form that shows ownership or close connection: whose car, whose book, whose room. Norwegian often uses "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "-s",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " for this, much like English uses apostrophe-s."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Add "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "-s",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " to the owner. The thing owned comes after it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Dette er lærerens bil."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "This is the teacher's car."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jeg leser Annas bok."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I am reading Anna's book."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "A definite noun is a noun marked as specific, like “the teacher” rather than “a teacher.” In Norwegian, the ending can carry that meaning: "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "læreren",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " means “the teacher,” and "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "lærerens",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " means “the teacher's.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Lærerens veske ligger på bordet."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The teacher's bag is on the table."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "The Owned Thing After -s",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "After the "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "-s",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " genitive, Norwegian usually puts the owned thing in the indefinite form. An indefinite noun is the basic “a” or bare form, like “a car” or “car,” not “the car.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Use owner + "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "-s",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " + indefinite owned noun: "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "lærerens bil",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", not "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "lærerens bilen",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Lærerens bil er rød."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The teacher's car is red."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Marias leilighet er liten."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Maria's apartment is small."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Barnets rom er lyst."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The child's room is bright."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "warning",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Do not add the definite ending to the owned noun after "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "-s",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": ". The owner carries the genitive marking; the owned noun stays indefinite."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "contrast",
      "title": "The til Pattern",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Norwegian can also show ownership with "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "til",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ": “to” or “belonging to” in this pattern. This is common in everyday speech and is especially clear when you want to say “the car of the teacher.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "In the "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "til",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " pattern, the owned noun comes first and is definite: "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "bilen til læreren",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Bilen til læreren står ute."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The teacher's car is outside."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Boka til Anna er interessant."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Anna's book is interesting."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Rommet til barnet er lyst."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The child's room is bright."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Both patterns can describe the same relationship. The form of the owned noun changes: after "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "-s",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " it is indefinite, but before "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "til",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " it is definite."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Lærerens bil er rød."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The teacher's car is red."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Bilen til læreren er rød."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The teacher's car is red."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "Names Ending in s, z, or x",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Most names simply take "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "-s",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". But when a name already ends in "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "s",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "z",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", or "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "x",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", Norwegian writes an apostrophe after the name instead of adding another "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "s",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Write "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Jens'",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", not "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Jenss",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jens' sykkel er ny."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jens's bike is new."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Alex' hund er rolig."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Alex's dog is calm."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "recap",
      "title": "Quick Recap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "To show ownership, choose one clear pattern and make the noun forms match that pattern."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Use owner + "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "-s",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " + indefinite owned noun: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "lærerens bil",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Use definite owned noun + "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "til",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " + owner: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "bilen til læreren",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "After names ending in "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "s",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "z",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", or "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "x",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", write only an apostrophe: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "Jens'",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Veska til Maria er svart."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Maria's bag is black."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
